WEBVTT

00:00:02.004 --> 00:00:08.266
Oxford Bookworms, Stage 1 The Monkeys Poor by W.W.

00:00:08.306 --> 00:00:19.890
Jacobs Chapter 1 It was cold and dark out in the road, and the rain did not stop for a minute.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:26.744
But in the little living-room of Number 12 Castle Road, it was nice and warm.

00:00:26.804 --> 00:00:34.357
Old Mr. White and his son Herbert played chess and Mrs. White sat and watched them.

00:00:34.416 --> 00:00:41.702
The old woman was happy because her husband and her son were good friends, and they liked to be together.

00:00:41.762 --> 00:00:45.565
Her but's a good son, she thought.

00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:51.930
We waited a long time for him, and I was nearly forty when he was born.

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:54.562
But we are a happy family.

00:00:54.622 --> 00:00:57.824
And old Mrs. White smiled.

00:00:57.884 --> 00:00:59.902
It was true.

00:00:59.962 --> 00:01:07.764
Herbert was young, and he laughed a lot, but his mother and his father laughed with him.

00:01:07.824 --> 00:01:13.818
They had not got much money, but they were a very happy little family.

00:01:13.878 --> 00:01:19.102
The two men did not talk because they played carefully.

00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:27.158
The room was quiet, but the noise of the rain was worse now, and they could hear it on the windows.

00:01:27.218 --> 00:01:31.102
Suddenly, old Mr. White looked up.

00:01:31.162 --> 00:01:34.814
Listen to the rain, he said.

00:01:34.874 --> 00:01:39.758
Yes, it's a bad night, Herbert answered.

00:01:39.818 --> 00:01:42.560
It's not a good night to be out.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:46.352
But is your friend Tom Morris coming tonight?

00:01:46.411 --> 00:01:49.093
Yes, that's right.

00:01:49.153 --> 00:01:53.276
He's coming at about seven o'clock, the old man said.

00:01:53.336 --> 00:01:56.235
But perhaps this rain?

00:01:56.295 --> 00:02:01.897
Mr. White did not finish, because just then the young man heard a noise.

00:02:01.917 --> 00:02:04.860
"'Listen,' Herbert said.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:07.082
"'There's someone at the door now.'

00:02:07.102 --> 00:02:12.626
"'I didn't hear a noise,' his father answered.

00:02:12.686 --> 00:02:17.651
But he got up from his chair and went to open the front door.

00:02:17.711 --> 00:02:22.706
Mrs. White got up too and began to put things away.

00:02:22.766 --> 00:02:26.380
Mr. White said, Come in!

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.341
Come in, Tom!

00:02:28.401 --> 00:02:31.372
It's wonderful to see you again.

00:02:31.432 --> 00:02:33.522
What a bad night!

00:02:33.582 --> 00:02:37.893
Give me your coat, and then come into the living room.

00:02:37.953 --> 00:02:41.154
It's nice and warm in there.

00:02:41.213 --> 00:02:49.236
The front door was open, and in the living room Mrs. White and Herbert felt the cold.

00:02:49.296 --> 00:02:55.732
Then Mr. White came back into the living room with a big red-faced man.

00:02:55.792 --> 00:03:01.110
"'This is Tom Morris,' Mr. White told his wife and son.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:04.453
"'We were friends when we were young.

00:03:04.473 --> 00:03:08.276
"'We worked together before Tom went to India.

00:03:08.296 --> 00:03:15.121
"'Tom, this is my wife, and this is our son, Herbert.

00:03:15.141 --> 00:03:19.564
"'Please to meet you,' Tom Morris said.

00:03:19.584 --> 00:03:25.583
"'Please to meet you, Mr. Morris,' Mrs. White answered.

00:03:25.643 --> 00:03:28.209
Please come and sit down.

00:03:28.269 --> 00:03:31.240
Yes, come on, Tom."

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.861
Mr. White said.

00:03:32.921 --> 00:03:36.872
Over here it's nice and warm.

00:03:36.932 --> 00:03:38.613
Thank you.

00:03:38.673 --> 00:03:41.384
The big man answered, and he sat down.

00:03:41.404 --> 00:03:46.426
"'Let's have some whiskey,' old Mr. White said.

00:03:46.446 --> 00:03:51.028
"'You need something to warm you on a cold night.'

00:03:51.088 --> 00:03:53.626
He got out a bottle of whiskey.

00:03:53.686 --> 00:03:58.176
and the two old friends began to drink and talk.

00:03:58.236 --> 00:04:11.106
The little family listened with interest to this visitor from far away, and he told them many strange stories.

00:04:11.166 --> 00:04:31.838
Chapter 2 After some time, Tom Morris stopped talking, and Mr. White said to his wife and son, Tom was a soldier in India for 21 years.

00:04:31.898 --> 00:04:35.440
India is a wonderful country.

00:04:35.499 --> 00:04:38.511
Yes, Herbert said.

00:04:38.571 --> 00:04:41.343
I'd like to go there.

00:04:41.363 --> 00:04:44.775
Oh, Herbert, his mother cried.

00:04:44.835 --> 00:04:49.758
She was afraid because she did not want to lose her son.

00:04:49.818 --> 00:04:53.162
I wanted to go to India too.

00:04:53.222 --> 00:05:01.381
Her husband said, but, it's better for you here, the soldier said quickly.

00:05:01.441 --> 00:05:06.826
But you saw a lot of strange and wonderful things in India.

00:05:06.886 --> 00:05:11.749
I want to see them two one day, Mr. White said.

00:05:11.809 --> 00:05:14.832
The soldier put down his whiskey.

00:05:14.892 --> 00:05:19.525
No, he cried, stay here.

00:05:19.585 --> 00:05:23.007
Old Mr. White did not stop.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:28.850
But your stories were interesting," he said to Tom Morris.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:34.093
What did you begin to say about a monkey's paw?

00:05:34.152 --> 00:05:37.874
Nothing, Morris answered quickly.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:41.957
Well, nothing important.

00:05:42.017 --> 00:05:46.480
A monkey's paw, Mrs. White said.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.750
Come on, Mr. Morris.

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:52.233
Tell us about it, Herbert said.

00:05:52.293 --> 00:05:59.298
Morris took his whiskey in his hand, but suddenly he put it down again.

00:05:59.357 --> 00:06:06.050
Slowly he put his hand into the pocket of his coat, and the white family watched him.

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:07.992
What is it?

00:06:08.052 --> 00:06:09.492
What is it?

00:06:09.552 --> 00:06:11.654
Mrs. White cried.

00:06:11.714 --> 00:06:14.415
Morris said nothing.

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:17.987
He took his hand out of his pocket.

00:06:18.046 --> 00:06:21.242
The white family watched carefully.

00:06:21.302 --> 00:06:27.440
And in the soldier's hand they saw something little and dirty.

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:36.386
Mrs. White moved back, afraid, but her son Herbert took it and looked at it carefully.

00:06:36.446 --> 00:06:39.698
Well, what is it?

00:06:39.758 --> 00:06:42.790
Mr. White asked his friend.

00:06:42.850 --> 00:06:46.584
Look at it, the soldier answered.

00:06:46.643 --> 00:06:48.836
It's a little poor.

00:06:48.895 --> 00:06:51.618
A monkey's poor.

00:06:51.678 --> 00:06:54.360
monkey's paw!"

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:57.382
Herbert said, and he laughed.

00:06:57.442 --> 00:07:02.075
Why do you carry a monkey's paw in your pocket, Mr. Morris?

00:07:02.135 --> 00:07:04.466
He asked the old soldier.

00:07:04.526 --> 00:07:12.000
Well, you see, Morris said, this monkey's paw is magic.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.542
Herbert laughed again.

00:07:14.602 --> 00:07:19.296
But the soldier said, don't laugh, boy.

00:07:19.355 --> 00:07:22.884
Remember, you're young.

00:07:22.944 --> 00:07:30.143
I'm old now, and in India I saw many strange things.

00:07:30.203 --> 00:07:41.215
He stopped talking for a minute, and then he said, This monkey's paw can do strange and wonderful things.

00:07:41.275 --> 00:07:45.706
An old Indian gave the paw to one of my friends.

00:07:45.766 --> 00:07:49.036
My friend was a soldier too.

00:07:49.096 --> 00:07:51.684
This paw is magic.

00:07:51.744 --> 00:07:56.835
Because it can give three wishes to three people.

00:07:56.894 --> 00:08:00.536
Who wonderful, Herbert said.

00:08:00.596 --> 00:08:06.560
But these three wishes don't bring happiness, the soldier said.

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:10.872
The old Indian wanted to teach us something.

00:08:10.932 --> 00:08:15.204
It's never good to want to change things.

00:08:15.263 --> 00:08:19.902
Well, did your friend have three wishes?

00:08:19.962 --> 00:08:22.840
Herbert asked the old soldier.

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:27.494
Yes, Morris answered quietly.

00:08:27.554 --> 00:08:33.488
And his third and last wish was to die.

00:08:33.548 --> 00:08:39.953
Mr. and Mrs. White listened to the story, and they felt afraid.

00:08:40.014 --> 00:08:44.696
But Herbert asked, and did he die?

00:08:44.756 --> 00:08:49.382
Yes, he did, Morris said.

00:08:49.442 --> 00:08:55.228
He had no family, so his things came to me when he died.

00:08:55.288 --> 00:09:02.792
The monkey's paw was with his things, but he told me about it before he died.

00:09:02.852 --> 00:09:06.204
Tom Morris finished quietly.

00:09:06.264 --> 00:09:09.546
What were his first two wishes then?

00:09:09.606 --> 00:09:11.348
Herbert asked.

00:09:11.408 --> 00:09:14.180
What did he ask for?

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:16.550
I don't know.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.978
He didn't want to tell me.

00:09:19.038 --> 00:09:21.615
The soldier answered.

00:09:21.675 --> 00:09:25.878
For a minute or two, everybody was quiet.

00:09:25.938 --> 00:09:33.954
But then Herbert said, and you, Mr. Morris, did you have three wishes?

00:09:34.014 --> 00:09:38.798
Yes, I did, Morris answered.

00:09:38.858 --> 00:09:40.760
I was young.

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:43.402
I wanted many things.

00:09:43.462 --> 00:09:45.744
A fast car.

00:09:45.804 --> 00:09:48.024
Money.

00:09:48.084 --> 00:09:53.805
Morris stopped for a minute, and then he said with difficulty.

00:09:53.865 --> 00:10:00.766
My wife and my young son died in an accident in the car.

00:10:00.826 --> 00:10:05.077
Without them, I didn't want the money.

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:08.978
So in the end, I wished to lose it.

00:10:09.038 --> 00:10:11.148
But it was too late.

00:10:11.208 --> 00:10:15.350
My wife and my child were dead.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:18.702
The room was very quiet.

00:10:18.762 --> 00:10:23.976
The White family looked at the unhappy face of the old soldier.

00:10:24.036 --> 00:10:30.590
Then Mr. White said, why do you want the paw now?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.841
You don't need it.

00:10:32.901 --> 00:10:35.622
You can give it to someone.

00:10:35.682 --> 00:10:38.744
How can I give it to someone?

00:10:38.805 --> 00:10:44.668
The soldier said, the monkey's paw brings unhappiness with it.

00:10:44.728 --> 00:10:48.722
Well, give it to me, Mr. White said.

00:10:48.782 --> 00:10:52.126
Perhaps this time it—No!"

00:10:52.186 --> 00:10:54.166
Tom Morris cried.

00:10:54.226 --> 00:10:56.287
You're my friend.

00:10:56.347 --> 00:10:59.458
I can't give it to you.

00:10:59.518 --> 00:11:06.130
Then after a minute he said, I can't give it to you.

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:10.680
But of course, you can take it from me.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:17.030
But remember, this monkey's paw brings unhappiness.

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:22.421
Old Mr. White did not listen, and he did not think.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:27.335
Quickly, he put out his hand, and he took the paw.

00:11:27.395 --> 00:11:33.840
Tom Morris looked unhappy, but Mr. White did not want to wait.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:36.733
What do I do now?

00:11:36.793 --> 00:11:38.814
He asked his friend.

00:11:38.874 --> 00:11:41.988
Yes, come on, father!

00:11:42.048 --> 00:11:47.227
Herbert said, make a wish, and he laughed.

00:11:47.287 --> 00:11:52.426
The soldier said nothing, and Mr. White asked him again.

00:11:52.486 --> 00:11:55.779
What do I do now?

00:11:55.839 --> 00:12:00.022
At first the old soldier did not answer.

00:12:00.082 --> 00:12:05.196
But in the end, he said quietly, OK.

00:12:05.256 --> 00:12:09.089
But remember, be careful.

00:12:09.150 --> 00:12:12.782
Think before you make your wish.

00:12:12.842 --> 00:12:17.265
Yes, yes, Mr. White said.

00:12:17.325 --> 00:12:23.248
Take the paw in your right hand, and then make your wish.

00:12:23.308 --> 00:12:26.570
But, Tom Morris began.

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:32.604
Yes, we know, Herbert said, be careful.

00:12:32.664 --> 00:12:39.468
Just then, Old Mrs. White stood up, and she began to get the dinner.

00:12:39.528 --> 00:12:41.950
Her husband looked at her.

00:12:42.010 --> 00:12:48.140
Then he smiled and said to her, come on, help me.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.358
What can I wish for?

00:12:50.418 --> 00:12:53.540
We need money, of course."

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.160
Mrs. White laughed.

00:12:56.220 --> 00:13:08.246
But she thought for a minute, and then she said, well, I'm getting old now, and sometimes it's difficult to do everything.

00:13:08.306 --> 00:13:12.548
Perhaps I need four hands and not two.

00:13:12.608 --> 00:13:18.188
Yes, ask the poor to give me two more hands.

00:13:18.248 --> 00:13:25.858
Okay then, her husband said, and he took the monkey's paw in his right hand.

00:13:25.918 --> 00:13:30.989
Everybody watched him, and for a minute he waited.

00:13:31.049 --> 00:13:34.930
Then he opened his mouth to make his wish.

00:13:34.990 --> 00:13:38.351
Suddenly Tom Morris stood up.

00:13:38.411 --> 00:13:41.672
Don't do it, he cried.

00:13:41.732 --> 00:13:45.152
The old soldier's face was white.

00:13:45.212 --> 00:13:47.716
Herbert and his mother laughed.

00:13:47.776 --> 00:13:51.351
but Mr. White looked at Tom's face.

00:13:51.411 --> 00:13:57.836
Old Mr. White was afraid, and he put the monkey's paw into his pocket.

00:13:57.896 --> 00:14:03.872
After a minute or two they sat down at the table and began to have dinner.

00:14:03.932 --> 00:14:09.566
The soldier told the family many strange and wonderful stories about India.

00:14:09.626 --> 00:14:12.198
They forgot the monkey's paw.

00:14:12.258 --> 00:14:19.296
And because the soldier's stories were interesting, They asked him many questions about India.

00:14:19.356 --> 00:14:24.800
When Tom Morris stood up to leave, it was very late.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:30.474
Thank you for a very nice evening, Morris said to the family.

00:14:30.534 --> 00:14:36.488
And thank you for a very good dinner, he said to Mrs. White.

00:14:36.548 --> 00:14:40.822
It was a wonderful evening for us, Tom.

00:14:40.882 --> 00:14:43.124
Old Mr. White answered.

00:14:43.184 --> 00:14:46.468
Your stories were very interesting.

00:14:46.528 --> 00:14:49.372
Our life isn't very exciting.

00:14:49.432 --> 00:14:52.484
And we don't have the money to visit India.

00:14:52.544 --> 00:14:55.506
So please come again soon.

00:14:55.566 --> 00:14:59.860
You can tell us some more stories about India.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:03.734
Then the old soldier put on his coat.

00:15:03.794 --> 00:15:13.004
He said goodbye to the white family and went out into the rain.

00:15:13.065 --> 00:15:22.876
Chapter 3 It was nearly midnight.

00:15:22.936 --> 00:15:30.614
In their warm living-room, the two old people and their sons sat and talked about the soldier's stories.

00:15:30.674 --> 00:15:35.548
India is a wonderful country, Mr. White said.

00:15:35.608 --> 00:15:37.970
What exciting stories!

00:15:38.031 --> 00:15:40.415
It was a good evening!

00:15:40.475 --> 00:15:44.780
Mrs. White stood up to take some things into the kitchen.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:48.561
But she stopped and listened to Herbert and his father.

00:15:48.621 --> 00:15:51.482
Yes, Herbert said.

00:15:51.542 --> 00:15:54.724
Morris told some interesting stories.

00:15:54.784 --> 00:15:58.356
But of course, some of them weren't true.

00:15:58.416 --> 00:16:00.306
Oh, Herbert!

00:16:00.366 --> 00:16:02.137
Mrs. White said.

00:16:02.197 --> 00:16:06.909
Well, mother, that story about the monkey's paw wasn't true.

00:16:06.929 --> 00:16:11.114
A dirty little monkey's paw isn't magic.

00:16:11.174 --> 00:16:13.358
But it was a good story."

00:16:13.418 --> 00:16:14.919
And Herbert smiled.

00:16:14.939 --> 00:16:21.223
"'Well, I think you're right, Herbert,' his mother said.

00:16:21.243 --> 00:16:26.546
"'I don't know,' Mr. White said quietly.

00:16:26.566 --> 00:16:29.868
"'Perhaps the story was true.

00:16:29.888 --> 00:16:34.562
"'Strange things can happen sometimes.'

00:16:34.622 --> 00:16:38.120
Mrs. White looked at her husband.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:42.748
Did you give some money to Tom Morris for that poor?"

00:16:42.808 --> 00:16:44.260
she asked.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:47.982
We don't have money to give away for nothing.

00:16:48.042 --> 00:16:50.934
Mrs. White was angry now.

00:16:50.994 --> 00:16:53.136
Well, yes.

00:16:53.196 --> 00:16:55.108
Her husband answered.

00:16:55.168 --> 00:16:56.638
I did.

00:16:56.698 --> 00:16:58.520
But not much.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.302
And at first he didn't want to take it.

00:17:01.362 --> 00:17:04.135
He wanted the monkey's poor.

00:17:04.195 --> 00:17:06.586
Well, he can't have it.

00:17:06.646 --> 00:17:08.214
Herbert laughed.

00:17:08.274 --> 00:17:13.793
It's our poor now, and we're going to be rich and happy.

00:17:13.853 --> 00:17:15.743
Come on, father.

00:17:15.803 --> 00:17:18.014
Make a wish.

00:17:18.074 --> 00:17:22.374
Old Mr. White took the paw from his pocket.

00:17:22.435 --> 00:17:24.835
OK, Herbert.

00:17:24.895 --> 00:17:27.896
But what am I going to ask for?

00:17:27.956 --> 00:17:29.806
I have everything.

00:17:29.866 --> 00:17:34.527
You, your mother, what do I need?

00:17:34.587 --> 00:17:36.726
Money, of course.

00:17:36.786 --> 00:17:38.816
Herbert answered quickly.

00:17:38.876 --> 00:17:40.187
We need money.

00:17:40.207 --> 00:17:43.618
You're always thinking about money.

00:17:43.678 --> 00:17:46.920
That's because we haven't got very much of it.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:50.912
With money, you can pay for this house.

00:17:50.972 --> 00:17:53.334
It can be your house.

00:17:53.394 --> 00:17:55.295
Go on, Father.

00:17:55.355 --> 00:17:58.968
Wish for thirty thousand pounds.

00:17:59.028 --> 00:18:04.640
Herbert stopped talking and his old father thought for a minute.

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:10.044
The room was quiet, and they could hear the rain on the windows.

00:18:10.104 --> 00:18:14.968
Then Mr. White took the monkey's paw in his right hand.

00:18:15.028 --> 00:18:20.322
He was afraid, but he looked at his wife and she smiled at him.

00:18:20.383 --> 00:18:23.866
Go on, she said.

00:18:23.926 --> 00:18:33.160
Slowly and carefully, Mr. White said, I wish for thirty thousand pounds.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:40.950
Suddenly he gave a cry, and Mrs. White and Herbert ran to him.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:43.340
What's the matter, Father?

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:44.921
Herbert asked.

00:18:44.981 --> 00:18:48.552
It moved, Mr. White cried.

00:18:48.612 --> 00:18:50.682
The monkey's paw!

00:18:50.742 --> 00:18:52.923
It moved!

00:18:52.983 --> 00:18:55.364
They looked at the paw.

00:18:55.424 --> 00:19:00.095
It was now on the floor and not in the old man's hand.

00:19:00.155 --> 00:19:03.760
The family watched it, and they waited.

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:06.547
but it did not move again.

00:19:06.607 --> 00:19:10.970
So the little family sat down again and they waited.

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:12.972
Nothing happened.

00:19:13.032 --> 00:19:21.469
The noise of the rain on the windows was worse now, and their little living-room did not feel nice and warm.

00:19:21.529 --> 00:19:25.442
Mrs. White said, It's cold.

00:19:25.502 --> 00:19:27.644
Let's go to bed.

00:19:27.704 --> 00:19:36.374
Mr. White did not answer, and in the end Herbert said, Well, There's no money, Father.

00:19:36.434 --> 00:19:39.586
Your friend's story wasn't true.

00:19:39.646 --> 00:19:42.406
But Mr. White did not answer.

00:19:42.466 --> 00:19:45.917
He sat quietly and said nothing.

00:19:45.977 --> 00:19:53.059
After some time, Mrs. White said to her husband, are you okay?

00:19:53.119 --> 00:19:54.830
Yes.

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:58.801
Yes, the old man answered.

00:19:58.861 --> 00:20:02.231
But for a minute or two, I was afraid.

00:20:02.292 --> 00:20:10.060
Well, We needed that money," Mrs. White said, but we aren't going to get it.

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.881
I'm tired.

00:20:11.941 --> 00:20:14.452
I'm going to bed.

00:20:14.512 --> 00:20:21.526
After Mrs. White went to bed, the two men sat and smoked for some time.

00:20:21.586 --> 00:20:27.908
Then Herbert said, well, Father, I'm going to bed too.

00:20:27.968 --> 00:20:31.510
Perhaps the money is in a bag under your bed.

00:20:31.570 --> 00:20:33.586
Good night, Father.

00:20:33.646 --> 00:20:38.086
and Herbert laughed and went out of the room.

00:20:38.146 --> 00:20:43.412
Old Mr. White sat in the cold living room for a long time.

00:20:43.472 --> 00:20:47.656
The candle died, and it was dark.

00:20:47.716 --> 00:20:52.650
Suddenly the old man saw a face at the window.

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:57.816
Quickly he looked again, but there was nothing there.

00:20:57.876 --> 00:21:00.030
He felt afraid.

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:10.576
Slowly he stood up and left the cold, dark room.

00:21:10.636 --> 00:21:27.217
Chapter 4 The next morning the winter sun came through the window and the house felt nice and warm again.

00:21:27.277 --> 00:21:33.028
Mr. White felt better, and he smiled at his wife and son.

00:21:33.088 --> 00:21:39.382
The family sat down to have breakfast, and they began to talk about the day.

00:21:39.442 --> 00:21:47.415
The monkey's paw was on a little table near the window, but nobody looked at it, and nobody thought about it.

00:21:47.435 --> 00:21:53.318
"'I'm going to the shops this morning,' Mrs. White said.

00:21:53.338 --> 00:21:57.107
"'I want to get something nice for dinner.

00:21:57.167 --> 00:21:59.526
Are you going to come with me?"

00:21:59.586 --> 00:22:01.536
she asked a husband.

00:22:01.596 --> 00:22:06.170
No, I'm going to have a quiet morning.

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:08.142
I'm going to read.

00:22:08.202 --> 00:22:10.222
Her husband answered.

00:22:10.282 --> 00:22:15.706
Well, I'm not going to go out this evening, Herbert said.

00:22:15.766 --> 00:22:18.508
So we can go to bed early tonight.

00:22:18.568 --> 00:22:21.434
We were very late last night.

00:22:21.494 --> 00:22:28.391
And we aren't going to have stories about monkey's paws," Mrs. White said.

00:22:28.451 --> 00:22:30.222
She was angry.

00:22:30.282 --> 00:22:33.343
Why did we listen to your friend?

00:22:33.403 --> 00:22:35.344
She asked her husband.

00:22:35.404 --> 00:22:39.055
A monkey's paw can't give you things.

00:22:39.115 --> 00:22:43.446
She stopped, but the two men did not answer her.

00:22:43.506 --> 00:22:48.428
Thirty thousand pounds, she said quietly.

00:22:48.488 --> 00:22:51.488
We needed that money.

00:22:51.548 --> 00:22:56.089
Just then Herbert looked at the clock and stood up.

00:22:56.149 --> 00:22:58.489
"'I'm going to work,' he said.

00:22:58.509 --> 00:23:02.570
"'Perhaps the postman has got the money for you in a letter.

00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:06.651
"'Remember, I want some of it too.'

00:23:06.711 --> 00:23:09.632
Herbert laughed, and his mother laughed too.

00:23:09.652 --> 00:23:13.572
"'Don't laugh, son,' Mr. White said.

00:23:13.592 --> 00:23:19.074
"'Tom Morris is an old friend, and he thinks the story is true.

00:23:19.094 --> 00:23:21.609
"'Perhaps it is.

00:23:21.669 --> 00:23:27.356
"'Well, leave some of the money for me,' Herbert laughed again.

00:23:27.416 --> 00:23:30.788
His mother laughed too, and she went to the door with him.

00:23:30.808 --> 00:23:35.150
"'Good-bye, mother,' Herbert said happily.

00:23:35.170 --> 00:23:38.751
"'Get something nice for dinner this evening at the shops.

00:23:38.771 --> 00:23:42.663
"'I'm always hungry after a day at work.

00:23:42.723 --> 00:23:47.185
"'I know you are,' Mrs. White answered.

00:23:47.245 --> 00:23:52.212
Herbert left the house and walked quickly down the road.

00:23:52.272 --> 00:23:56.378
His mother stood at the door for some time and watched him.

00:23:56.438 --> 00:24:06.161
The winter sun was warm, but suddenly she felt very cold.

00:24:06.221 --> 00:24:16.994
CHAPTER V Slowly, old Mrs. White went back into the house.

00:24:17.054 --> 00:24:21.504
Her husband looked up and saw something strange in her face.

00:24:21.564 --> 00:24:24.394
"'Watch the matter,' he asked.

00:24:24.414 --> 00:24:31.176
"'Nothing,' his wife answered, and she sat down to finish her breakfast.

00:24:31.236 --> 00:24:41.739
She began to think about Tom Morris again, and suddenly she said to her husband, "'Your friend drank a lot of whiskey last night!

00:24:41.799 --> 00:24:43.840
Her monkeys pour!

00:24:43.900 --> 00:24:46.150
To what a story!'

00:24:46.211 --> 00:24:51.852
Mr. White did not answer her, because just then the postman arrived.

00:24:51.913 --> 00:24:57.286
He brought two letters for them, but there was no money in them.

00:24:57.346 --> 00:25:03.590
After breakfast the two old people forgot about the money and the monkey's paw.

00:25:03.650 --> 00:25:13.726
Later in the day, at about one o'clock, Mr. and Mrs. White sat down to eat, and then they began to talk about money again.

00:25:13.786 --> 00:25:19.189
They did not have very much money, so they often needed to talk about it.

00:25:19.249 --> 00:25:23.933
That's thirty thousand pounds, Mrs. White said.

00:25:23.993 --> 00:25:25.844
We need it.

00:25:25.904 --> 00:25:28.576
But it didn't come this morning.

00:25:28.635 --> 00:25:30.186
Her husband answered.

00:25:30.246 --> 00:25:32.168
Let's forget it.

00:25:32.228 --> 00:25:34.029
Then he said.

00:25:34.090 --> 00:25:36.461
But that thing moved.

00:25:36.521 --> 00:25:39.883
The monkey's paw moved in my hand.

00:25:39.943 --> 00:25:42.614
Tom's story was true.

00:25:42.674 --> 00:25:46.047
You drank a lot of whiskey last night.

00:25:46.107 --> 00:25:49.319
Perhaps the paw didn't move.

00:25:49.379 --> 00:25:51.060
Mrs. White answered.

00:25:51.120 --> 00:25:52.640
It moved!

00:25:52.700 --> 00:25:55.402
Mr. White cried angrily.

00:25:55.462 --> 00:26:03.716
At first his wife did not answer, but then she said, well, Herbert laughed about it.

00:26:03.776 --> 00:26:06.528
Suddenly she stopped talking.

00:26:06.588 --> 00:26:09.420
She stood up and went over to the window.

00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:11.180
What's the matter?

00:26:11.240 --> 00:26:13.142
Her husband asked.

00:26:13.202 --> 00:26:17.804
There's a man in front of our house, Mrs. White answered.

00:26:17.864 --> 00:26:19.475
He's a stranger.

00:26:19.535 --> 00:26:22.406
very tall and well dressed.

00:26:22.466 --> 00:26:25.136
He's looking at our house.

00:26:25.196 --> 00:26:26.807
Oh, no.

00:26:26.867 --> 00:26:28.337
It's OK.

00:26:28.397 --> 00:26:30.298
He's going away.

00:26:30.358 --> 00:26:32.638
Come and sit down.

00:26:32.698 --> 00:26:36.239
Finish eating, Mr. White said.

00:26:36.299 --> 00:26:40.320
The old woman did not listen to her husband.

00:26:40.380 --> 00:26:42.821
He isn't going away.

00:26:42.881 --> 00:26:44.121
She went on.

00:26:44.181 --> 00:26:46.092
He's coming back.

00:26:46.152 --> 00:26:48.236
I don't know him.

00:26:48.296 --> 00:26:50.202
He's a stranger.

00:26:50.262 --> 00:26:51.522
Yes.

00:26:51.582 --> 00:26:53.722
He's very well dressed.

00:26:53.782 --> 00:26:56.363
Suddenly Mrs. White stopped.

00:26:56.423 --> 00:26:58.213
She was very excited.

00:26:58.274 --> 00:27:00.544
He's coming to the door.

00:27:00.604 --> 00:27:03.064
Perhaps he's bringing the money.

00:27:03.125 --> 00:27:07.066
And she ran out of the room to open the front door.

00:27:07.125 --> 00:27:10.966
The tall well dressed stranger stood there.

00:27:11.026 --> 00:27:13.117
But a minute, he said nothing.

00:27:13.177 --> 00:27:14.888
But then he began.

00:27:14.948 --> 00:27:16.933
Good afternoon.

00:27:16.994 --> 00:27:20.352
I'm looking for Mr. and Mrs. White."

00:27:20.412 --> 00:27:24.504
Well, I'm Mrs. White," the old woman answered.

00:27:24.564 --> 00:27:26.806
What can I do for you?

00:27:26.866 --> 00:27:36.434
At first the stranger did not answer, but then he said, Mrs. White, I'm from Moore and Megan's.

00:27:36.494 --> 00:27:39.526
Can I come in and talk to you?

00:27:39.586 --> 00:27:46.227
Moore and Megan's had a big factory, and Herbert White worked there on the machinery.

00:27:46.287 --> 00:27:49.805
"'Yes, of course,' Mrs. White answered.

00:27:49.825 --> 00:27:52.026
"'Please come in.'

00:27:52.086 --> 00:27:57.948
The well-dressed stranger came into the little living room and Mr. White stood up.

00:27:57.968 --> 00:28:01.220
"'Are you Mr. White?'

00:28:01.280 --> 00:28:03.231
the stranger began.

00:28:03.290 --> 00:28:04.631
Then he went on.

00:28:04.651 --> 00:28:08.322
"'I'm from morned Megan's.'

00:28:08.382 --> 00:28:11.854
Mrs. White looked at the stranger and she thought.

00:28:11.874 --> 00:28:15.268
"'Perhaps he has the money.

00:28:15.328 --> 00:28:18.312
but why warned Megan's?

00:28:18.372 --> 00:28:21.284
And his face is very unhappy.

00:28:21.344 --> 00:28:23.055
Why?

00:28:23.115 --> 00:28:26.878
Suddenly the old woman was afraid.

00:28:26.938 --> 00:28:29.208
Please sit down.

00:28:29.268 --> 00:28:31.049
Mr. White began.

00:28:31.110 --> 00:28:33.691
But now his wife could not wait.

00:28:33.751 --> 00:28:35.352
What's the matter?

00:28:35.412 --> 00:28:36.792
She cried.

00:28:36.852 --> 00:28:38.534
Is Herbert?

00:28:38.594 --> 00:28:41.336
She could not finish the question.

00:28:41.396 --> 00:28:44.582
The stranger did not look at their faces.

00:28:44.642 --> 00:28:47.147
and Mr. White began to be afraid to.

00:28:47.167 --> 00:28:50.529
"'Please tell us,' he said.

00:28:50.549 --> 00:28:57.362
"'I'm very sorry,' the man from Moore and Meghan's began.

00:28:57.423 --> 00:29:01.135
He stopped for a minute, and then he began again.

00:29:01.155 --> 00:29:08.359
"'I'm very sorry, but this morning there was an accident at the factory.

00:29:08.379 --> 00:29:10.940
"'What's the matter?

00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:13.031
Is Herbert okay?'

00:29:13.091 --> 00:29:15.422
Mrs. White cried again.

00:29:15.482 --> 00:29:19.994
Well, the man began slowly.

00:29:20.054 --> 00:29:22.084
Is he in hospital?

00:29:22.144 --> 00:29:25.675
The old woman asked, very afraid now.

00:29:25.735 --> 00:29:33.546
Yes, but the stranger looked at Mrs. White's face and stopped.

00:29:33.606 --> 00:29:36.236
Is he dead?

00:29:36.297 --> 00:29:39.297
Is Herbert dead?

00:29:39.357 --> 00:29:41.887
Mr. White asked quietly.

00:29:41.947 --> 00:29:43.168
Dead?

00:29:43.228 --> 00:29:44.828
Mrs. White cried.

00:29:44.888 --> 00:29:45.954
Oh, no!

00:29:46.014 --> 00:29:47.320
Please!

00:29:47.380 --> 00:29:49.100
Not dead!

00:29:49.160 --> 00:29:50.881
Not Herbert!

00:29:50.941 --> 00:29:53.531
Not our son!"

00:29:53.591 --> 00:29:59.462
Suddenly the old woman stopped because she saw the stranger's face.

00:29:59.522 --> 00:30:02.333
Then the two old people knew.

00:30:02.393 --> 00:30:05.463
Their son was dead.

00:30:05.523 --> 00:30:11.884
Old Mrs. White began to cry quietly, and Mr. White put his arm round her.

00:30:11.944 --> 00:30:20.782
Some time later the man from Moen Meghan said, It was the machinery, an accident.

00:30:20.842 --> 00:30:23.444
Herbert called help.

00:30:23.504 --> 00:30:27.688
The men heard him, and ran to him quickly.

00:30:27.748 --> 00:30:29.870
But they could do nothing.

00:30:29.930 --> 00:30:36.074
The next minute he was in the machinery, I'm very, very sorry.

00:30:36.134 --> 00:30:38.155
He finished.

00:30:38.216 --> 00:30:42.288
For a minute or two, the room was quiet.

00:30:42.348 --> 00:30:48.530
At last, Mrs. White said, dead.

00:30:48.590 --> 00:30:51.302
We're never going to see him again.

00:30:51.362 --> 00:30:54.524
What are we going to do without him?"

00:30:54.585 --> 00:30:56.656
Her husband said.

00:30:56.716 --> 00:30:58.978
He was our son.

00:30:59.038 --> 00:31:01.450
We loved him.

00:31:01.510 --> 00:31:04.972
Then Mrs White asked the stranger.

00:31:05.032 --> 00:31:07.124
Can we see him?

00:31:07.184 --> 00:31:09.305
Can we see our son?

00:31:09.365 --> 00:31:11.406
Please take me to him.

00:31:11.466 --> 00:31:13.768
I want to see my son.

00:31:13.828 --> 00:31:16.672
But the stranger answered quickly.

00:31:16.732 --> 00:31:18.694
No, he said.

00:31:18.754 --> 00:31:21.205
It's better not to see him.

00:31:21.265 --> 00:31:24.627
They couldn't stop the machinery quickly.

00:31:24.687 --> 00:31:27.518
He was in there for a long time.

00:31:27.578 --> 00:31:30.269
And at first they couldn't get him out.

00:31:30.330 --> 00:31:33.491
He was the man stopped.

00:31:33.552 --> 00:31:37.744
Then he said, don't go to see him.

00:31:37.804 --> 00:31:44.519
The stranger went over to the window because he did not want to see the faces of the two old people.

00:31:44.580 --> 00:31:50.194
He said nothing, but he stood there for some time and he waited.

00:31:50.254 --> 00:31:56.019
Then he went back to the old people and began to talk again.

00:31:56.079 --> 00:31:59.662
There's one more thing, he said.

00:31:59.722 --> 00:32:05.744
Your son worked for more and Meggins for six years, and he was a good worker.

00:32:05.804 --> 00:32:10.984
Now more and Megan's want to help you at this unhappy time."

00:32:11.044 --> 00:32:14.076
Again the stranger stopped.

00:32:14.136 --> 00:32:17.368
After a minute he began again.

00:32:17.428 --> 00:32:21.732
More and Megan's want to give you some money.

00:32:21.792 --> 00:32:25.294
Then he put something into Mr. White's hand.

00:32:25.354 --> 00:32:29.398
Old Mr. White did not look at the money in his hand.

00:32:29.458 --> 00:32:34.608
Slowly he stood up and looked at the stranger, afraid.

00:32:34.668 --> 00:32:36.686
How much?"

00:32:36.746 --> 00:32:39.840
Mr. White asked very quietly.

00:32:39.900 --> 00:32:50.611
He did not want to hear the answer.

00:32:50.671 --> 00:33:07.864
Three days later, in the big new cemetery two miles from their house, the two old people said goodbye to their dead son.

00:33:07.924 --> 00:33:11.806
Then they went back to their dark old house.

00:33:11.866 --> 00:33:20.012
They did not want to live without Herbert, but they waited for something good to happen, something to help them.

00:33:20.072 --> 00:33:23.336
The days went by very slowly.

00:33:23.396 --> 00:33:32.322
Sometimes they did not talk because there was nothing to say without Herbert, and so the days felt very long.

00:33:32.382 --> 00:33:40.428
Then one night, about a week later, Mrs. White got out of bed because she could not sleep.

00:33:40.489 --> 00:33:45.422
She sat by the window and she watched and waited for her son.

00:33:45.482 --> 00:33:49.786
He did not come and she began to cry quietly.

00:33:49.846 --> 00:33:56.224
In the dark her husband heard her, and he called, come back to bed.

00:33:56.284 --> 00:33:58.798
It's cold out there.

00:33:58.858 --> 00:34:03.252
It's colder for my son, his wife answered.

00:34:03.312 --> 00:34:06.786
He's out there in the cold cemetery.

00:34:06.846 --> 00:34:10.281
Mrs. White did not go back to bed.

00:34:10.341 --> 00:34:15.354
But Mr. White was old and tired, and the bed was warm.

00:34:15.415 --> 00:34:18.716
So in the end he went to sleep again.

00:34:18.776 --> 00:34:22.038
Suddenly he heard a cry from his wife.

00:34:22.098 --> 00:34:24.599
The poor, she cried.

00:34:24.659 --> 00:34:26.830
The monkey's poor!

00:34:26.890 --> 00:34:30.252
She came back to the bed and stood there.

00:34:30.312 --> 00:34:31.963
What is it?

00:34:32.023 --> 00:34:33.634
What's the matter?

00:34:33.694 --> 00:34:35.474
Mr. White cried.

00:34:35.535 --> 00:34:37.445
He sat up in bed.

00:34:37.506 --> 00:34:39.207
What's the matter?

00:34:39.267 --> 00:34:40.413
He thought.

00:34:40.473 --> 00:34:42.530
Why is she excited?

00:34:42.590 --> 00:34:44.761
What's she talking about?

00:34:44.821 --> 00:34:46.782
He looked at his wife.

00:34:46.842 --> 00:34:50.223
Her face was very white and the dark.

00:34:50.283 --> 00:34:53.935
I want it, she said quietly.

00:34:53.995 --> 00:34:55.775
And you've got it.

00:34:55.836 --> 00:34:57.286
Give it to me.

00:34:57.346 --> 00:34:58.827
Please!

00:34:58.887 --> 00:35:00.118
What?

00:35:00.178 --> 00:35:01.798
Mr. White asked.

00:35:01.858 --> 00:35:03.889
The monkey's paw!

00:35:03.949 --> 00:35:05.150
Mrs. White said.

00:35:05.210 --> 00:35:06.611
Where is it?

00:35:06.671 --> 00:35:10.654
It's downstairs," Mr. White answered.

00:35:10.714 --> 00:35:11.444
Why?

00:35:11.464 --> 00:35:15.866
Mrs. White began to laugh and cry.

00:35:15.926 --> 00:35:19.599
We could have two more wishes, she cried.

00:35:19.659 --> 00:35:23.341
We had one, but there are two more.

00:35:23.401 --> 00:35:24.782
Oh, no!

00:35:24.842 --> 00:35:25.852
Not again!

00:35:25.872 --> 00:35:27.633
Think, woman!

00:35:27.693 --> 00:35:29.484
Mr. White cried.

00:35:29.544 --> 00:35:32.136
But Mrs. White did not listen.

00:35:32.196 --> 00:35:36.565
Quickly, she said, go and get the paw.

00:35:36.626 --> 00:35:41.416
We're going to wish for our boy to come back to us."

00:35:41.436 --> 00:35:41.866
No.

00:35:41.926 --> 00:35:43.447
Mr. White cried.

00:35:43.507 --> 00:35:44.898
You're mad.

00:35:44.958 --> 00:35:46.079
Get it.

00:35:46.139 --> 00:35:47.740
Get it quickly.

00:35:47.800 --> 00:35:50.062
Mrs. White cried again.

00:35:50.122 --> 00:35:53.684
Mr. White said again, think, woman.

00:35:53.744 --> 00:35:55.004
Think.

00:35:55.064 --> 00:35:59.328
Our boy was in the machinery for a long time.

00:35:59.388 --> 00:36:02.170
They didn't want to show him to us.

00:36:02.230 --> 00:36:03.480
Think.

00:36:03.540 --> 00:36:06.310
Do you want to see his body?

00:36:06.370 --> 00:36:09.010
Yes, he's my son.

00:36:09.030 --> 00:36:12.675
I'm not afraid of him," she answered.

00:36:12.735 --> 00:36:22.250
You don't understand, Mr. White said sadly, but he went downstairs to look for the monkey's paw.

00:36:22.310 --> 00:36:27.988
In the living room it was dark, and Mr. White did not have a candle.

00:36:28.049 --> 00:36:33.942
Slowly he went across the room, and he put out his hand for the monkey's paw.

00:36:34.002 --> 00:36:38.136
He touched it, and quickly took his hand away again.

00:36:38.196 --> 00:36:39.527
No!

00:36:39.587 --> 00:36:40.608
he thought.

00:36:40.668 --> 00:36:42.279
I can't.

00:36:42.340 --> 00:36:44.891
I don't want to see Herbert.

00:36:44.951 --> 00:36:50.255
His face, after he was in the machinery, no!

00:36:50.315 --> 00:36:53.106
Then he thought about his wife.

00:36:53.166 --> 00:36:56.755
and he put out his hand and took the paw.

00:36:56.816 --> 00:36:59.946
In the bedroom, his wife waited.

00:37:00.006 --> 00:37:04.727
She saw the paw in Mr. White's hand and cried, quick!

00:37:04.787 --> 00:37:06.747
Make the wish!

00:37:06.807 --> 00:37:08.678
I can't!

00:37:08.738 --> 00:37:10.388
Mr. White answered.

00:37:10.448 --> 00:37:11.888
Remember!

00:37:11.948 --> 00:37:14.839
He died in the machinery!

00:37:14.899 --> 00:37:16.709
Make the wish!

00:37:16.769 --> 00:37:19.830
I'm not afraid of my own son!

00:37:19.890 --> 00:37:22.278
Mrs. White cried again.

00:37:22.338 --> 00:37:36.031
Mr. White looked sadly at his wife, but he took the poor in his right hand and said slowly, I wish for my son, Herbert, to come back to us.

00:37:36.091 --> 00:37:39.592
Then he sat down in the nearest chair.

00:37:39.652 --> 00:37:44.704
But Mrs. White went over to the window and looked out into the road.

00:37:44.764 --> 00:37:49.406
She stayed there for a long time, and she did not move.

00:37:49.466 --> 00:37:51.438
Nothing happened.

00:37:51.498 --> 00:37:53.810
The monkey's paw could not do it."

00:37:53.830 --> 00:38:00.472
"'Thank God,' Mr. White said, and he went back to bed.

00:38:00.532 --> 00:38:07.844
Soon Mrs. White went to bed, too."

00:38:07.904 --> 00:38:17.037
Chapter 7 But they did not sleep.

00:38:17.097 --> 00:38:20.208
They waited, and they listened.

00:38:20.268 --> 00:38:26.532
In the end Mr. White got up to get a candle because the dark made him more afraid.

00:38:26.592 --> 00:38:33.906
He began to go downstairs, but suddenly he heard a noise at the front door.

00:38:33.966 --> 00:38:36.739
He stopped, and he listened.

00:38:36.799 --> 00:38:38.810
He could not move.

00:38:38.870 --> 00:38:41.462
Then the noise came again.

00:38:41.522 --> 00:38:43.313
This time he ran.

00:38:43.374 --> 00:38:48.895
He ran upstairs, back into the bedroom, and he closed the door behind him.

00:38:48.955 --> 00:38:52.224
But again, the noise came.

00:38:52.284 --> 00:38:53.964
What's that?

00:38:54.024 --> 00:38:57.616
Mrs. White cried, and she sat up in bed.

00:38:57.676 --> 00:38:58.946
Nothing.

00:38:59.006 --> 00:39:01.217
Go to sleep again.

00:39:01.277 --> 00:39:03.418
Her husband answered.

00:39:03.478 --> 00:39:05.698
But Mrs. White listened.

00:39:05.758 --> 00:39:08.119
And the noise came again.

00:39:08.179 --> 00:39:09.880
It's Herbert.

00:39:09.940 --> 00:39:12.381
It's Herbert, she cried.

00:39:12.441 --> 00:39:15.292
I'm going to open the door for him.

00:39:15.352 --> 00:39:19.658
And she got out of bed and ran to the door of the bedroom.

00:39:19.718 --> 00:39:23.695
Mr. White got there first and stopped her.

00:39:23.715 --> 00:39:23.996
No!

00:39:24.056 --> 00:39:25.046
he cried.

00:39:25.106 --> 00:39:26.146
Think!

00:39:26.206 --> 00:39:28.168
But it's my boy!

00:39:28.228 --> 00:39:29.539
It's Herbert!"

00:39:29.599 --> 00:39:31.280
she answered.

00:39:31.300 --> 00:39:31.560
No!

00:39:31.620 --> 00:39:32.851
Don't go!

00:39:32.911 --> 00:39:34.062
Don't!

00:39:34.122 --> 00:39:36.464
Her husband cried again.

00:39:36.524 --> 00:39:39.295
But Mrs. White did not listen to him.

00:39:39.355 --> 00:39:42.978
She opened the bedroom door and ran from the room.

00:39:43.038 --> 00:39:44.978
I'm coming, Herbert!

00:39:45.038 --> 00:39:46.280
I'm coming!

00:39:46.340 --> 00:39:47.652
she called.

00:39:47.712 --> 00:39:49.996
Mr. White ran after her.

00:39:50.056 --> 00:39:51.007
Stop!

00:39:51.067 --> 00:39:52.048
He cried.

00:39:52.108 --> 00:39:53.399
Remember!

00:39:53.459 --> 00:39:56.281
Herbert died in the machinery!

00:39:56.341 --> 00:39:59.123
You don't want to see him!

00:39:59.184 --> 00:40:03.967
For a minute Mrs. White stopped and looked at her husband.

00:40:04.027 --> 00:40:09.051
But then the noise came again, and she began to run downstairs.

00:40:09.111 --> 00:40:10.702
Help me!

00:40:10.762 --> 00:40:12.373
Help me!

00:40:12.434 --> 00:40:14.536
She called to her husband.

00:40:14.596 --> 00:40:17.382
But Mr. White did not move.

00:40:17.442 --> 00:40:19.859
The paw, he thought.

00:40:19.919 --> 00:40:22.710
Where's the monkey's paw?

00:40:22.770 --> 00:40:25.482
He ran back into the bedroom.

00:40:25.542 --> 00:40:27.424
Quick, he thought.

00:40:27.484 --> 00:40:28.894
Where is it?

00:40:28.954 --> 00:40:32.146
At first he could not find it in the dark.

00:40:32.206 --> 00:40:34.228
Ah, there it was.

00:40:34.288 --> 00:40:35.508
He had it.

00:40:35.569 --> 00:40:39.852
Just at that minute he heard his wife downstairs.

00:40:39.912 --> 00:40:40.972
Wait!

00:40:41.032 --> 00:40:42.443
Wait, Herbert!

00:40:42.503 --> 00:40:43.664
I'm coming!

00:40:43.724 --> 00:40:44.884
She cried.

00:40:44.944 --> 00:40:47.982
She began to open the front door.

00:40:48.042 --> 00:40:56.924
At the same time, Mr. White took the monkey's paw in his right hand, and he made his third wish.

00:40:56.984 --> 00:41:03.839
Mrs. White gave a long unhappy cry, and her husband ran down to her.

00:41:03.899 --> 00:41:06.882
She stood by the open door.

00:41:06.942 --> 00:41:08.982
Very afraid.

00:41:09.042 --> 00:41:13.065
Old Mr. White looked out into the dark.

00:41:13.126 --> 00:41:17.188
The road was dark and quiet.

00:41:17.248 --> 00:41:19.113
and there was nobody there.

